{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"783b7f20db413410c32a97ff6c0e8097b09e1e11f42507ffef317c7a361cdd87","digest":{"component_or_area":"test_subcall_class_selection.py — model-provenance guards","key_entities":["tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py","_run_request_sites","_verdict","_parsed","_functions","run_request_sites","test_the_provenance_analysis_can_see_the_sites_it_judges","test_no_run_request_inherits_the_raw_config_model","test_every_unfollowable_site_is_registered_with_a_reason","test_neither_registry_has_stale_entries","src/rebar","RunRequest","ast.parse"],"problem_keywords":["test performance","redundant analysis","AST parsing","repetition","caching"],"propositions":["Four model-provenance guard tests each invoke _run_request_sites(), which performs identical whole-tree AST analysis across the src/rebar source, causing repeated and expensive re-parsing","Within each _run_request_sites() call, _verdict's parameter-provenance branch re-walks the entire tree and re-parses every file once per parameter-provenance site, and _functions() re-parses the whole tree again, causing per-file parses to occur ~8,033 times in a single scan","Caching _run_request_sites() result in a session-scoped pytest fixture reduces invocation from 4 to 1 per test process","Memoizing per-path AST parsing with functools.cache reduces single-scan duration by 65% and eliminates redundant read-parse cycles across _run_request_sites, _functions, and _verdict"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787352374256900001,"uuid":"dfd5a0f1-148f-4bd7-9456-d45766dafaf3"}